<p>Leaders from government and industry met in New Delhi for India’s AI Impact Summit 2026. Semafor, citing The Economist, said the gathering was India’s chance to “hype itself as an emerging AI power” and show it can convene the world’s AI players. Beyond the symbolism, the summit brought a run of partnership announcements and investment plans involving major AI firms and Indian conglomerates. A key diplomatic thread was global rulemaking for AI. NDTV reported Swiss President Guy Parmelin traveled to India for the summit as India and Switzerland spotlighted their efforts to help shape international AI governance. Parmelin later said the next AI Impact Summit will be held in Geneva in 2027. The summit also produced a lighter viral moment: during a staged photo op with Prime Minister Narendra Modi and other leaders, OpenAI CEO Sam Altman and Anthropic CEO Dario Amodei—standing beside each other—didn’t clasp hands as others did.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/KuilsA209FpB5m8PHDtQ8nt2mfxJItmfsSLGCAd2GdNsPxi0sGgPwS79d8kgcz_X883jn0zYM27WYLsJI4-hFvFEmLlvA2p3L65IhvL0T62j8G-9MdmHxYcWKFaq06QLG_Z1MJPc0TJpCvRW2y3ujyzWs_t2zKNyuA-iVn_Dddv8nMygSGoVdQGezxY-NT4U7A' alt='Switzerland’s President Guy Parmelin speaks during the AI Impact Summit in New Delhi.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Corporate tie-ups: Anthropic announced a partnership with Infosys, while OpenAI worked with Mumbai-based Tata Group on data center plans—another sign of India’s growing role in AI infrastructure and services.</li><li>Data center bet: Reliance Industries put a $110 billion data center investment plan on the table at the summit, one of the event’s biggest headline figures in its dealmaking push.</li><li>Bilateral framing: NDTV called India and Switzerland’s relationship “friendly and multifaceted,” and Parmelin’s two-day visit added momentum to their joint work on global AI rules.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Government of India: India used the summit to position itself as an emerging AI power and a global convener, bringing political and business leaders to New Delhi. (<a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/02/19/2026/india-ai-summit-attracts-money-and-rivals'>Semafor</a>)</li><li>Switzerland (President Guy Parmelin): Parmelin said smaller countries should work together so AI’s benefits are widely shared, and he announced that Geneva will host the 2027 AI Impact Summit. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/sci-tech/technology/next-ai-impact-summit-will-be-held-in-geneva-says-switzerlands-president/article70652671.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>OpenAI and Anthropic leadership: Altman and Amodei declined to clasp hands during Modi’s staged photo op, a visual nod to rivalry at a summit meant to bring competitors under one roof. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/asia/south-asia/article/3344074/openai-and-anthropic-ceos-refuse-hold-hands-during-modis-india-ai-summit-photo-op'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/asia/south-asia/article/3344074/openai-and-anthropic-ceos-refuse-hold-hands-during-modis-india-ai-summit-photo-op'>OpenAI and Anthropic CEOs refuse to hold hands during Modi’s India AI summit photo op</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/02/19/2026/india-ai-summit-attracts-money-and-rivals'>India AI summit attracts money and rivals</a> - semafor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/india-news/india-switzerland-shape-global-ai-rules-as-swiss-president-guy-parmelin-pm-modi-meet-at-ai-impact-summit-11094634#publisher=newsstand'>India, Switzerland Shape Global AI Rules As Leaders Meet At AI Impact Summit</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/sci-tech/technology/next-ai-impact-summit-will-be-held-in-geneva-says-switzerlands-president/article70652671.ece'>Switzerland’s President announces Geneva as host of 2027 AI Impact Summit</a> - thehindu.com</li></ul>